# Documentation map

This project uses **Durable Project Memory** to preserve knowledge across
sessions, agents, and time.

| Question | Canonical source |
| --- | --- |
| What must the project do now? | Living Spec-Driven Development (SDD) contracts in `docs/specs/` |
| Why was this approach selected? | Architecture Decision Records (ADRs) in `docs/adr/` |
| When was work proposed and delivered? | GitHub Issues, PRs, and commits |
| Does the behavior still hold? | Test-Driven Development (TDD), Behavior-Driven Development (BDD), CI, and release evidence |
| Where should an agent start? | `AGENTS.md` and this page |

Projects updated from an older template may still own `docs/decisions/`.
Search it alongside `docs/adr/`; write new records to `docs/adr/`, and never
move or overwrite existing project content automatically.

